# Comic Project Structure Guide

## Main Files
The main entry point is [index.html](mdc:index.html), which contains the core structure of the comic creation application. Styling is managed through [src/styles/main.css](mdc:src/styles/main.css).

## UI Components
The application uses several key UI components:

### Canvas Size Selection
- Located in the upload page section
- Uses `.canvas-size-selection` class for styling
- Contains horizontally aligned buttons in `.button-row` for selecting canvas dimensions:
  - DEFAULT 1:1 (700x700px)
  - Amazon KDP (7"x10")

### Upload Section
- Styled with `.upload-section` class
- Contains image upload functionality and library management
- Includes `.upload-area` for drag-and-drop functionality
- `.image-library` displays uploaded images in a grid layout

### Editor Interface
- Main editing area uses `.editor-container` class
- Sidebar navigation with `.editor-sidebar` class
- Comic panels styled with `.comic-panel` class
- Text bubble system with various styles (speech, thought, caption)

## Style Guidelines
- Primary buttons use `.primary-btn` class
- Active states indicated with `.active` or `.selected` classes
- Consistent color scheme defined in CSS root variables

- Responsive design breakpoints at 1400px and 1200px